II. Prove that simultaneous shearing in both directions (x and y) is not equal to the composition of pure shear along x-(3)axis followed by pure shear along y-axis.III. Specif the significance of continuity conditions. Discuss paramefiic continuity conditions and differentiate it with 1geometric continuity condition. (0.5+1.5+l) ISECTION C (Attempt any two)I. What is Projection? Differentiate Parallel and Perspective projection. A unit cube is projected on to the xy plane findout the coordinate ofthe projected image using perspective projection, ifcenter ofprojection is (0, 0, l0). (l+l+3)II. Rotate a triangle at A (0, 0), B (l,l), C (5,2) by 450 about the point p Cl,-l). (j)III. Find the coordinates of a pyramid whose coordinates are A(0,0,0), B( I ,0,0), C(0, I ,0) and D(0,0, I ) after mirrorreflection with respect to the plane passing through the origin, and having the normal vector N: i+j+j. (5)

